# venv Python dependencies (top-level)
#
# Policy (Option A, settled 2026-05-23):
#   - venv-managed: scientific stack (numpy/scipy/matplotlib/pandas/PyQt5) +
#     mujoco + transitive + cython + ruff + colcon build tooling
#   - Inherited via --system-site-packages: rclpy / ament_* (ROS 2 Jazzy),
#     python3-bt2 (kernel-bound), python3-colcon-* / python3-vcstool /
#     python3-rosdep (system bootstrap tools)
#
# Why scientific stack moved venv-side: avoid cross-workspace collisions when
# another control project on the same host pins a different numpy/scipy
# version. venv pin wins sys.path priority. Trade-off: ros-jazzy-rclpy is
# built against numpy 1.x ABI, so numpy<2 must remain pinned until ROS 2
# Kilted (numpy 2.x baseline). Bump only with rclpy import smoke test.
#
# Lock generation:
#   uv pip compile requirements.in --generate-hashes -o requirements.lock
#
# Sync on a new machine: ./install.sh 가 수행 (install_python.sh 의 ensure_venv +
#   install_python_deps). 손으로 할 때의 명령, 그리고 --python 을 버전이 아니라
#   경로로 줘야 하는 이유: README.md "Python 의존성 sync".

# Scientific stack — pinned to apt-jazzy baseline for rclpy ABI compatibility
numpy<2
scipy
matplotlib
pandas
PyQt5

# Simulation + build tooling
mujoco==3.7.0
Cython==3.2.4
ruff==0.15.20
# colcon-core 0.20.1 호환 (PEP 660 editable installs)
setuptools<80
wheel
